{"BlockedEmail.should_block? performs non-atomic read-increment-save of match_count, causing lost increments under concurrent signup requests": 0.8054137229919434, "validate_each calls BlockedEmail.should_block?(value) without guarding against nil or blank values, causing NoMethodError when value =~ regexp is called on nil email values during validation": 0.6181660890579224, "rejectedEmails array is initialized once on the controller prototype and never cleared, causing valid emails to be incorrectly blocked if they match previously rejected values across signup attempts": 0.4997117519378662, "Signup failure response exposes raw validation errors via user.errors.to_hash and echoes user-provided values back, potentially leaking internal validation details and creating XSS risk if rendered unsafely": 0.33953672647476196, "Frontend only checks result.errors.email but ActiveModel::Errors#to_hash may not include email key if validation failed on different attribute, breaking the client-side blocked email recording logic": 0.11322622001171112, "Comment stating last_match_at indicates whether emails have ever been blocked is now inaccurate since it's updated for any match attempt including action_type :do_nothing records": 0.0997098833322525}